				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Cocoon): Update CHANGELOG with v2.2 release and improved narrative\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing Cocoon's CHANGELOG in line with Mountain's prose format. The v2.2 section documents the bundled-electron correctness pass: parent-PID watchdog for orphan detection, -32004 benign-404 classification for file-not-found errors, FileWatcher.Register benign classifier, and BuildOpenTextDocument UTF-8 decoding fix enabling positionAt for npm extension scripts.\n\nHistorical version entries (v2.1, v2.0, v1.3, v1.2, v1.1) have been restructured from bullet-point lists to narrative paragraphs explaining architectural motivation and impact of each release cycle.\n\nAligns with the prose-style CHANGELOG format established in Mountain, improving consistency across the Land project components.",
			"SHA": "393741b596e74135f876781d0d2260e285e68a43"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T05:16:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Sync CHANGELOG to prose format, add v2.2 section\n\nSubmodule synchronization updating Mountain to 9515b2f7. The CHANGELOG has been restructured from itemized bullet points to narrative prose paragraphs, improving readability while preserving all historical content. A new v2.2 section documents the bundled-electron correctness pass including JSON-RPC -32004 for benign 404s, deferred-no-op file watching, canonical-path comparison for Volume mounts, Identifier field on SCM provider DTO, sky:replay-events handler, 64KB terminal ring buffer, and tree:getChildren timeout reduction.\n\nThe new prose format emphasizes user-facing impact over file references, making it more useful for release notes and external communication.",
			"SHA": "119c3acaa6851f09e4df23bca9835f43a9bf060b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T04:58:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Sync submodules with terminal event bridging and search schema migration\n\nMulti-component synchronization restoring terminal rendering and search functionality:\n\n1. **Output**: Bridge localPty channel events through Tauri's sky:// event system - Add ChannelEventBridge to map VS Code's IPC `channel.listen()` calls to Tauri's native event system. The localPty channel now routes `onProcessData`, `onProcessReady`, and `onProcessExit` events from Mountain's PTY reader to the workbench's terminal service handlers. Previously, `channel.listen()` returned a no-op handler that silently discarded all event subscriptions, causing the terminal's xterm panel to stay blank despite Mountain emitting `sky://terminal/data` hundreds of times.\n\n2. **Sky**: Migrate search result format to VS Code ≥1.92 schema - VS Code ≥1.92 renamed the search result shape: `preview.text` → `previewText`, `preview.matches` + `ranges` → `rangeLocations[]` with `{source, preview}` pairs. Stock vscode's `searchResult.add()` reads the new fields and silently rejects entries with the old shape. This transforms Mountain's ripgrep results into the current `ITextSearchMatch` format, restoring search functionality.\n\n3. **Cocoon**: Submodule synchronization to latest downstream.\n\nImpact: Terminals now render properly. Search panel now displays results (was showing 0 despite 2560 line-matches).",
			"SHA": "8273c1268659fc3a973f289a7162ac7a49cc5de6"
		}
	],
